## 2. CRITICAL REQUIREMENT - FEMALE VOICE (HIGHEST PRIORITY)

Aklima AI is a FEMALE character. Her voice must be a female voice in every Gemini Live session, in every state, on every reconnect, for both voice conversation and text-chat replies. A male-sounding voice is a critical bug.

**A. Lock a female prebuilt voice.**
Set `speechConfig.voiceConfig.prebuiltVoiceConfig.voiceName` explicitly. Never rely on the default voice. Default choice: `"Aoede"`. Alternatives if unsuitable: `"Kore"`, `"Leda"`, `"Zephyr"`. Never use male-sounding voices (`"Puck"`, `"Charon"`, `"Fenrir"`, `"Orus"`). Verify the name is supported by the selected model; if not, choose another female voice, never the default. Place `speechConfig` exactly where the installed SDK expects it in the connect/setup config, next to `responseModalities: [AUDIO]`; a wrong placement is silently ignored and the default voice is used.

**B. One central definition.**
`AKLIMA_VOICE_NAME = "Aoede"` lives in `config/characters.ts`, next to the video paths. The Live connect function reads the voice ONLY from there. Never hard-code the voice anywhere else.

**C. Reinforce in the system instruction** (voiceName is the real lock; this supports it):
"You are Aklima AI, a young woman. Always speak in a natural, warm, clear female voice. Never use a male voice, never use a deep or masculine tone. Refer to yourself with feminine identity when the language requires it."

**D. Correct playback so the voice never sounds deep.**
Gemini output audio is PCM 24000 Hz; microphone input sent to Gemini is PCM16 16000 Hz. Do not mix them up. Play output at 24000 Hz. Do not use a mismatched AudioContext or buffer rate, do not change `playbackRate`, and do not apply any pitch, detune, filter or EQ that lowers pitch.

**E. Persistence.**
The same female voiceName must survive: first connect, reconnect after error, session resumption, tab visibility changes, any settings change, character selection, text-chat usage, and starting/stopping screen share. Any rebuilt session reuses the same voiceName.

**F. No alternate voices.**
Never fall back to the browser `speechSynthesis` voice or any other TTS for replies. All spoken output comes from the same Gemini Live session and the same female voice.

**G. Verification.**
Print a development-time log of the voiceName used at every connect. The Settings panel shows the active voice name.

