## 4. STATE MODEL (ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH)

```ts
type AssistantState  = "idle" | "listening" | "thinking" | "speaking" | "error";
type ConnectionState = "disconnected" | "connecting" | "connected";
type VisualState     = "idle" | "thinking" | "speaking"; // derived, never set by the video itself
type ScreenShareState = "off" | "requesting" | "starting" | "active" | "paused" | "stopping" | "error";
```

- `AssistantState` and `ConnectionState` live in `state/assistantStore.ts`. `ScreenShareState` lives in its own `screenShareStore` and is NEVER mixed into the others.
- `VisualState` mapping: idle / listening / error / disconnected -> `idle`; thinking -> `thinking`; speaking -> `speaking`.
- UI labels, glow, waveform and video are all derived from this one source. The video component never decides state.
- Labels: Disconnected "Tap to talk"; Connecting "Connecting..."; Listening "Listening"; Thinking "Thinking..."; Speaking "Aklima AI is speaking"; Error "Connection lost. Tap to reconnect."

