## 5. INPUT MODES (VOICE + TEXT, ONE SESSION)

Both modes share the SAME single Gemini Live session, the same female voice, the same audio queue, the same video state machine. Never create a second session, a second AI path, a `generateContent` text pipeline, or a separate TTS.

### 5.1 Voice mode (primary, voice-first)
- Large central microphone button. Tap to start: connects if needed, requests mic permission, starts streaming 16 kHz PCM16 mono. Tap again to stop the microphone only (the session stays alive so chat keeps working). A separate "Disconnect" action lives in Settings.
- Natural conversation, no push-to-talk. Voice activity and interruption per Section 7.

### 5.2 Text chat mode (secondary, reply is spoken)
- A **Chat** button next to the microphone opens a compact glass chat sheet (Section 10). Closed by default.
- Flow: user types and sends -> if not connected, connect automatically (microphone permission is NOT required for text chat) -> send the text through the Live session's realtime text input (verify the exact method in the installed SDK; for current Live models this is the realtime text input method, and the older client-content method may be limited to seeding history) -> `thinking` state and thinking video immediately -> Aklima AI's reply arrives as audio -> `speaking` when audio actually plays -> reply text appears in the chat sheet in sync with the audio.
- **The written reply and the spoken reply are the same response.** Enable input and output audio transcription in the Live config (verify field names) and render the output transcription as the assistant's text message. The user must always hear the reply as female-voice audio, whether they spoke or typed.
- If the user sends text while Aklima AI is speaking, treat it as an interruption: stop playback, clear the queue, then process the new text.
- If the user speaks while the chat sheet is open, show their spoken words (input transcription) as a message marked with a mic icon, and the reply as text plus audio.
- Output control: a "Read replies aloud" toggle (default ON) implemented as a gain/mute on the output node only. It must never change sample rate, pitch, voice or the session.
- The first user gesture (Send tap or mic tap) must resume/unlock the AudioContext so audio is never blocked by browser autoplay policy.
- Screen share + text: if sharing is active, send the latest useful frame (forced send) right before the text so questions like "What's on my screen?" typed in chat work too.

