## 7. AUDIO PIPELINE (`audio/`)

**Capture (AudioStreamer):** `getUserMedia` -> AudioContext (AudioWorklet preferred) -> resample -> PCM16 / 16 kHz / mono -> chunks -> Gemini. Handles permission, init, resampling, conversion, chunking, streaming, cleanup (stop all tracks on stop).

**Playback (AudioPlayer):** Gemini audio chunks -> PCM decode -> gapless scheduled queue -> AudioContext at 24000 Hz -> speaker. No `playbackRate` change, no pitch effects (Section 2D). Smooth streaming, no gaps between chunks.

**Real playback state drives the UI:**
- Speaking begins only when assistant audio is actually scheduled/playing, not when a response event arrives.
- Speaking ends when the queue is empty and the last source has ended.
- An analyser node feeds the waveform and audio-level meter.

**Interruption:** if the user speaks (or sends text) while Aklima AI is speaking: stop playback immediately, clear the queue, stop the speaking video, switch to listening (idle video), keep the session and screen share alive, prioritize the user. Never keep the speaking video after an interruption.

**Thinking detection:** after user speech ends (or text is sent) enter `thinking` and stay there until playable audio actually starts. If Gemini is slow, keep the thinking video; never freeze or show an empty screen.

