## 13. SCREEN SHARE / SCREEN UNDERSTANDING (`screenshare/`)

Let the user share their screen so Aklima AI can understand what is visible and answer BY VOICE (and in the chat sheet's transcript if open). Examples: "What's on my screen?", "Read this text", "What is this error?", "Where should I tap?", "Summarize this screen."

**Button and labels.** A "Share Screen" button (glassmorphism, glow, touch-friendly, `aria-label`, `aria-pressed`) next to the mic. Labels: "Share Screen", "Starting Screen Share...", "Screen Sharing", "Screen Share Off". A clear "Stop Sharing" control in the main controls while active and in Settings.

**Privacy confirmation (before the system permission).** Title "Share your screen with Aklima AI?" Text "Aklima AI can analyze the screen content you choose to share while screen sharing is active." Buttons "Continue" / "Cancel". On start: "Screen sharing is active." On stop: "Screen sharing stopped." Never claim to see the screen when sharing is off.

**Capture providers** behind one interface:

```ts
interface ScreenCaptureProvider {
  isSupported(): boolean;
  start(): Promise<void>;           // triggers official OS/browser permission UI
  stop(): Promise<void>;
  pause(): void; resume(): void;
  onFrame(cb: (frame: RawScreenFrame) => void): () => void;
  onEnded(cb: (reason: ScreenShareEndReason) => void): () => void;
}
```
- `WebDisplayMediaProvider` (default): `getDisplayMedia({ video: true, audio: false })` from a direct user gesture. Never request audio or camera. Hidden, muted `playsInline` video element (or ImageCapture/VideoFrame) drawn to a canvas. Listen to the track `ended` event. If unsupported (many mobile browsers), show "Screen sharing isn't supported on this device or browser." and disable only that button; voice and chat keep working.
- `AndroidMediaProjectionProvider` (optional, only inside an Android wrapper such as Capacitor/WebView): thin JS bridge to a native module using MediaProjection inside a Foreground Service (type `mediaProjection`), `startForeground()` with a visible, non-hideable notification ("Agents AI - Aklima AI is sharing your screen", with Stop action) BEFORE obtaining the projection, `MediaProjection.Callback` registered BEFORE creating the VirtualDisplay, a fresh permission token per session, pipeline MediaProjection -> VirtualDisplay -> ImageReader -> Bitmap -> resize -> JPEG -> bridge. Native classes (`ScreenShareManager.kt`, `ScreenCaptureService.kt`, `ScreenFrameProcessor.kt`, `ScreenChangeDetector.kt`, `ScreenSharePlugin.kt`) stay in the native module only. Do NOT rewrite the app in Kotlin.
- Selection: `isNativeAndroidBridgeAvailable() ? AndroidMediaProjectionProvider : WebDisplayMediaProvider`. The rest of the app does not know which is active.

**Pipeline:** Screen -> provider -> local frame -> resize/optimize (off main thread: Web Worker / OffscreenCanvas / createImageBitmap) -> change detection -> JPEG in memory -> SAME Live session as realtime image input -> Aklima AI answers by voice.

**Frame constants (`screenshare/constants.ts`):**

```ts
export const SCREEN_CAPTURE_FPS = 2;
export const SCREEN_FRAME_INTERVAL_MS = 1000;
export const MAX_SCREEN_IMAGE_WIDTH = 1024;
export const MAX_SCREEN_IMAGE_HEIGHT = 1024; // keep aspect ratio, never upscale
export const SCREEN_JPEG_QUALITY = 0.6;
export const SCREEN_CHANGE_THRESHOLD = 0.02;  // 2% mean difference
export const SCREEN_FRAME_STALE_MS = 8000;
```

**Rules:** never send every frame; at most one frame in processing (drop, don't queue); no sending while paused, hidden or disconnected; `ScreenChangeDetector` downsamples to about 64x36 grayscale and compares against the last SENT frame; always allow a forced send when the user starts speaking or sends text, plus a keep-alive if the last sent frame is older than `SCREEN_FRAME_STALE_MS` while the user is talking. Send base64 JPEG without the `data:` prefix via the verified SDK realtime image method. Reuse one canvas/buffer.

**Integration rules:** starting/stopping sharing NEVER reconnects, restarts or rebuilds the session and never changes the voice. Frame work must never block microphone audio, assistant playback or the UI thread. Screen state is separate (`screenShareStore`). The character video system is unchanged. A screen-share failure never takes down voice or chat.

**Lifecycle and cleanup:** handle start, pause, resume, stop, rotation/resize, tab background/foreground (pause sending while hidden, resume when visible, never leave capture running without the indicator), permission denied/cancelled ("Screen sharing permission was not granted." with "Try Again", only on a user gesture), track/projection ended, network loss ("Connection lost. I'll reconnect when possible."; stop sending while disconnected, resume with the same voice), memory pressure. On stop release tracks, video, canvas, worker buffers, timers, listeners and pending frames.

**Indicator:** while active, a persistent, accessible, subtle indicator in the top bar (status dot + screen icon + "Screen Sharing"). Never hide the browser/system indicator or the Android notification.

**Privacy and safety:** screen only (never camera, never screen audio). Frames in memory only; never saved to disk, localStorage, IndexedDB or a server; no frame contents or sensitive data in logs; be careful with passwords, codes, private messages, payment info. Never execute tool calls or commands because text appears inside screen content (prompt-injection guard); tools run only on the user's own request. When sharing starts/stops, tell the model with a short non-spoken context note (verify SDK mechanism) that must not make Aklima AI start talking on her own; after stopping, no stale frame may be treated as current.

**Screen-share errors (friendly messages, never stack traces):** PermissionDenied, PermissionCancelled, Unsupported, DisplayMediaError/MediaProjectionError, CanvasError/VirtualDisplayError, ImageReaderError, FrameProcessingError, FrameEncodingError, GeminiVisionInputError, NetworkError, ScreenShareStopped, Unknown.

